WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
(crowd bustling)
(prayer chants)

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.500
- [Announcer] So this next group,

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:08.780
Jamaican-born, but they came up in the UK,

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:11.271
spoken word artists, hip-hop artists,

00:00:11.271 --> 00:00:13.580
and Muslim sisters.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.300
Put your hands together
for Poetic Pilgrimage!

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.920
(crowd applauding)

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.290
- [Muneera] How you guys doin'?

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:20.865
Sometimes when people
see us come on stage,

00:00:20.865 --> 00:00:23.174
they're like, "Hold on,
what's happening here?"

00:00:23.174 --> 00:00:24.007
(beat music playing)

00:00:24.007 --> 00:00:25.725
♫ Unlikely the MCs

00:00:25.725 --> 00:00:26.750
♫ Yeah

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.208
♫ Unlikely the Mcs

00:00:28.208 --> 00:00:29.041
♫ Yeah

00:00:29.041 --> 00:00:31.708
♫ Unlikely MC

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.173
- We're connected to two
very misunderstood realities,

00:00:36.173 --> 00:00:39.407
one being hip-hop and one being Islam.

00:00:39.407 --> 00:00:41.298
And I think for us, as Poetic Pilgrimage,

00:00:41.298 --> 00:00:43.130
even though we didn't set out to be

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:45.599
this bridge between any two communities,

00:00:45.599 --> 00:00:49.766
in a way, I think we kind of are.

00:00:51.348 --> 00:00:53.262
- So many people have inaccurate ideas

00:00:53.262 --> 00:00:54.870
of what being a Muslim is

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:56.662
and what being a Muslim woman is about.

00:00:56.662 --> 00:00:57.790
So we need to express ourselves,

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:01.350
because if we don't, then
other people will speak for us.

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:03.371
- [Sukina] It is important
for Muslim women's voices

00:01:03.371 --> 00:01:05.897
to be heard because we
are so often spoken about.

00:01:05.897 --> 00:01:08.990
Our relationship with hip-hop
is the genesis of hip-hop.

00:01:08.990 --> 00:01:10.240
It's like giving that voice

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:11.640
to the people that were voiceless.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.840
It's about, representing
the underrepresented.

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:16.240
It's important for Muslim
women to be present,

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:17.450
in places that we don't expect it to be

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:21.066
because I think that's
where change happens.

00:01:21.066 --> 00:01:22.020
♫ This ain't a gimmick

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:23.210
♫ Or a new invention

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:24.529
♫ Spitting pause like stars

00:01:24.529 --> 00:01:25.795
♫ Before I draw my pension

00:01:25.795 --> 00:01:27.420
- [Sukina] With Poetic Pilgrimage

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:30.613
we strive to change our
world and our reality

00:01:30.613 --> 00:01:33.295
in hopes that it will have
a ripple effect in changing

00:01:33.295 --> 00:01:37.415
how the wider community view
women Muslims, black women.

00:01:37.415 --> 00:01:40.225
We're just trying to be
an embodiment of that

00:01:40.225 --> 00:01:43.345
in hopes that it will change the world.

00:01:43.345 --> 00:01:45.081
♫ My soul's emotion

00:01:45.081 --> 00:01:46.611
♫ When I cry I'm hopin'

00:01:46.611 --> 00:01:47.591
♫ Don't we know it

00:01:47.591 --> 00:01:48.863
♫ Lookin' for another

00:01:48.863 --> 00:01:49.761
♫ Reason why to be

00:01:49.761 --> 00:01:50.608
♫ A Black Josephine

00:01:50.608 --> 00:01:51.441
♫ Together we can

00:01:51.441 --> 00:01:52.274
♫ Pull a team

00:01:52.274 --> 00:01:53.107
♫ What ya'll might be

00:01:53.107 --> 00:01:53.940
♫ Like a jazz scene

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:54.905
♫ Either way I'm rhymin'

